# File: tests/features/add_greeting_ends_with_name_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/71-add-greeting-ends-with-name-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Add greeting_ends_with_name library helper
  As a maintainer exercising nmg-sdlc against this disposable Python host
  I want a public greeting_ends_with_name(name) library helper
  So that callers can observe whether the generated greeting ends with the supplied name while retaining the existing greeting and CLI contracts

  @SCN001
  Scenario: A valid name returns the greeting suffix result
    Given the installed package is importable
    When greeting_ends_with_name is called with Ada
    Then it returns True
    And that value equals greet Ada endswith Ada

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A different valid name uses that same name
    Given the installed package is importable
    When greeting_ends_with_name is called with Jo
    Then it returns True
    And that value equals greet Jo endswith Jo
    And the result is not specific to the Ada example

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Invalid names preserve greet validation
    Given greeting_ends_with_name is imported from the public package
    When greeting_ends_with_name is called with a blank, whitespace-only, or non-string name
    Then it raises ValueError with message name must not be blank
    And that error is the existing greet validation error, not a wrapped or renamed error

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Existing greeting and CLI behavior remains unchanged
    Given the distribution is installed
    When greet is called with Ada
    Then it returns Hello, Ada
    When nmg-smoke Ada is run
    Then the process exits 0 and prints Hello, Ada followed by a single newline
    And blank names still raise ValueError from greet and still cause the CLI to exit non-zero without a stdout greeting
